WEBVTT

00:01.470 --> 00:06.040
<i>I still remember the shock I felt then.</i>

00:07.240 --> 00:12.190
<i>The harsh reality that slammed 
into me without warning.</i>

00:18.690 --> 00:21.950
<i>The warm hand that once patted my head.</i>

00:23.660 --> 00:28.460
<i>The kind smile that once soothed my heart.</i>

00:28.870 --> 00:31.390
<i>That strong, gentle person</i>

00:31.960 --> 00:34.570
<i>who worked harder than 
anyone I'd ever known...</i>

00:35.400 --> 00:38.180
<i>That someone like him should 
be denied his dream...</i>

00:38.780 --> 00:40.520
<i>It was an undeniable injustice.</i>

00:41.650 --> 00:44.230
<i>I'm not without my own feelings of guilt.</i>

00:45.730 --> 00:47.020
<i>But...</i>

00:47.710 --> 00:51.780
<i>To defeat him... the person 
I can never forgive...</i>

00:52.350 --> 00:56.200
<i>I need a stronger half inside 
me to support the brittle one.</i>

00:57.280 --> 01:01.110
<i>To face the true goal that lies ahead...</i>

01:11.510 --> 01:17.310
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:21.370 --> 02:27.920
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:34.350 --> 02:36.500
Isn't this an amazing sight?

02:35.220 --> 02:37.640
<b>#9 A Disquieting Beginning</b>

02:36.500 --> 02:38.590
You didn't see it last year?

02:38.820 --> 02:41.470
Well, I saw a little bit,

02:41.470 --> 02:45.470
but I was way more focused 
on hanging with my friends.

02:46.760 --> 02:49.570
It almost doesn't feel real.

02:49.570 --> 02:53.360
Yeah, you don't get many chances 
to ride on a cruise ship.

02:53.660 --> 02:55.580
Not that part.

02:55.580 --> 02:58.110
I mean the part where we're dating.

02:58.610 --> 03:01.860
You're just totally 
hopeless with this stuff.

03:02.530 --> 03:04.570
So, what about you?

03:04.930 --> 03:07.210
Has it sunk in for you yet?

03:08.210 --> 03:10.460
I'm not sure.

03:10.810 --> 03:14.600
It has for part of me, 
and for another part, it hasn't.

03:14.600 --> 03:16.250
What does that mean?

03:16.250 --> 03:19.240
I just never thought we'd 
be able to meet outside

03:19.240 --> 03:21.500
like this without anyone knowing.

03:21.890 --> 03:23.370
Yeah, I guess.

03:23.850 --> 03:27.650
Depending on what they reveal 
about the rules of the special test,

03:27.650 --> 03:30.250
I may ask you to do some things.

03:30.580 --> 03:32.110
Yeah, I've got it.

03:32.680 --> 03:35.510
Assuming it's stuff I can handle, anyway.

03:37.870 --> 03:40.150
Looks like the first-years are done.

03:40.540 --> 03:43.810
We can't go in together, 
so I'll go on ahead.

03:52.830 --> 03:55.040
Why are you sitting <i>there</i>?!

03:55.040 --> 03:57.280
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

03:57.280 --> 03:58.380
Of course not.

03:58.740 --> 04:01.100
Why do I have to—

04:03.540 --> 04:07.550
I will now explain the rules of 
the deserted island special test.

04:07.970 --> 04:09.520
For two weeks, starting tomorrow,

04:09.520 --> 04:13.310
you will undergo a survival test 
where you compete for game points.

04:13.620 --> 04:16.390
If everyone on your team 
drops out, you fail at once.

04:16.390 --> 04:19.570
The bottom five placers 
will be expelled at once.

04:19.570 --> 04:22.370
There are two ways to score game points.

04:22.370 --> 04:24.080
One is through movement.

04:24.080 --> 04:26.100
The map is divided into 100 squares,

04:26.100 --> 04:28.730
and you can acquire game points by 
moving into designated areas within.

04:29.050 --> 04:33.320
Designated areas will be announced four 
times per day at designated times.

04:33.720 --> 04:35.530
There are rules regarding 
area designation.

04:35.530 --> 04:38.750
Three of the designated areas will be 
within two spaces horizontal or vertical,

04:38.750 --> 04:41.470
or one space diagonal, of each other.

04:41.470 --> 04:45.270
However, once per day, there will 
be a random area designated

04:45.270 --> 04:47.220
in an unpredictable location.

04:47.700 --> 04:49.970
Game points will be assigned 
in order of arrival:

04:49.970 --> 04:54.150
ten for first place, 
five for second, three for third.

04:54.150 --> 04:55.730
One bonus point will be given

04:56.100 --> 04:59.020
to anyone who arrives in the 
area within the time limit,

04:59.430 --> 05:00.700
but arrival order rewards

05:00.700 --> 05:04.240
will only be awarded once all 
members of the group have arrived.

05:04.630 --> 05:08.990
If you are already within an 
area when it is designated,

05:09.210 --> 05:10.920
each person present will earn one point,

05:10.920 --> 05:12.750
but the arrival order
 reward will not apply.

05:13.170 --> 05:16.140
If you neglect to arrive at 
three designated areas in a row,

05:16.140 --> 05:17.750
you will be penalized.

05:17.750 --> 05:21.290
Before I explain the other 
way to get game points,

05:21.290 --> 05:22.680
I want you to look at this.

05:23.570 --> 05:26.960
You'll wear these watches 
throughout the test,

05:26.960 --> 05:29.990
and you will be given synced tablets.

05:29.990 --> 05:32.740
These are what will 
record your game points,

05:32.740 --> 05:34.520
so keep them with you at all times.

05:34.890 --> 05:38.610
In addition, your health will 
be constantly monitored,

05:38.610 --> 05:42.910
and if you exceed safe baselines, 
an alarm will sound.

05:43.940 --> 05:46.910
It's designed to stop automatically 
after five seconds,

05:46.910 --> 05:51.090
but if you remain in the red zone, 
the alarm will sound again.

05:52.070 --> 05:56.250
If your problematic condition continues, 
it will turn into an emergency alarm.

05:56.840 --> 06:00.920
If this happens, you must receive a 
medical check in the starting area,

06:01.290 --> 06:03.540
but if you can't make it there,

06:03.540 --> 06:06.550
you will be penalized appropriately, 
with disqualification on the table.

06:06.850 --> 06:10.060
If the emergency alarm continues 
for over five minutes,

06:10.060 --> 06:13.540
a team of teachers and medical staff 
will follow the GPS to your location.

06:13.860 --> 06:16.180
If you attempt to remove 
the watch by force,

06:16.560 --> 06:18.260
or if it suffers a mechanical failure,

06:18.260 --> 06:20.440
the scoring function will turn off.

06:20.730 --> 06:21.830
If that happens,

06:21.830 --> 06:24.210
you will need to return to the 
starting area to swap your equipment.

06:24.710 --> 06:26.810
Let's return to the movement scoring.

06:27.160 --> 06:31.700
All groups will not necessarily have the 
same designated areas during the test.

06:32.180 --> 06:35.560
The watches are programmed 
with twelve different tables.

06:36.020 --> 06:37.060
Your designated areas

06:37.060 --> 06:40.820
from the first to last day will be 
determined in advance by these tables.

06:41.480 --> 06:44.830
Of course, all members of a 
group will have the same table,

06:44.830 --> 06:48.840
and if you form a large group, your 
tables will be changed to match.

06:49.230 --> 06:51.180
The second way of scoring game points

06:51.180 --> 06:54.970
is by performing challenges set 
at various places on the island.

06:55.550 --> 06:58.760
The nature of these challenges and 
where they spawn will be unpredictable.

06:59.100 --> 07:01.550
You can view challenge information, 
including participation conditions,

07:01.550 --> 07:03.190
but you will not be able to see

07:03.190 --> 07:05.730
their current status until 
you physically arrive.

07:05.980 --> 07:09.770
Food and water will be included 
among the challenge rewards.

07:10.150 --> 07:14.260
If you wish to join up with another 
group, you must link up your watches.

07:15.500 --> 07:20.760
I would now like to ask Acting Chairman 
Tsukishiro to say a few words.

07:26.500 --> 07:28.200
This is Tsukishiro.

07:28.200 --> 07:30.070
This deserted island test

07:30.070 --> 07:34.140
may be the largest special test 
our school has ever undertaken.

07:35.170 --> 07:39.980
I want to warn you about 
what you will be facing.

07:40.520 --> 07:43.610
The school, in its capacity 
as your caretakers,

07:43.610 --> 07:46.770
will monitor you as best we can.

07:46.770 --> 07:52.030
But on an island of this size, 
our surveillance cannot be perfect.

07:52.260 --> 07:57.220
Any instances of sexual abuse will 
be penalized without hesitation,

07:57.640 --> 08:01.690
and truly vile behavior may 
result in legal action.

08:02.600 --> 08:04.230
And one more thing...

08:04.600 --> 08:08.740
As hunger and thirst can 
quickly lead to frustration,

08:08.740 --> 08:11.570
we may see fights between students.

08:12.360 --> 08:18.020
I intend to be relatively 
permissive of this.

08:18.510 --> 08:23.310
In practice, I feel it would be 
impossible to prevent any conflict at all.

08:23.310 --> 08:28.710
Of course, with anything truly vile, 
the school will get involved.

08:29.100 --> 08:32.270
Depending on the nature of the activity, 
you may be forced to drop out,

08:32.620 --> 08:35.140
and you may be expelled.

08:36.060 --> 08:37.560
That is all.

08:38.070 --> 08:43.130
I hope that you will act in 
ways befitting the students of

08:43.130 --> 08:44.730
Advanced Nurturing High School.

08:48.180 --> 08:51.340
Thank you, Acting Chairman Tsukishiro.

08:52.150 --> 08:53.450
To conclude,

08:53.450 --> 08:58.270
I will explain the provisions and 
tools you will need for the island.

09:01.660 --> 09:04.540
Whoa, awesome!

09:04.540 --> 09:06.600
Is this enough for everyone?

09:07.540 --> 09:08.600
What?

09:08.600 --> 09:12.380
I guess this is difficult for both of us.

09:12.830 --> 09:15.050
Charging into that crowd feels so awkward.

09:15.050 --> 09:18.490
What? Please. I'm nothing like you.
I can easily handle this!

09:22.740 --> 09:24.120
What are you doing?

09:24.120 --> 09:26.250
I wanna make sure...

09:26.250 --> 09:31.550
we have... the water... we need!

09:33.300 --> 09:35.370
<i>Water is certainly precious.</i>

09:33.930 --> 09:35.740
What are you doing?

09:35.740 --> 09:38.250
<i>I'll either have to collect 
rainwater on-site</i>

09:36.550 --> 09:39.980
My back!

09:38.250 --> 09:41.050
<i>or complete challenges to get it.</i>

09:55.310 --> 09:57.070
Did you sleep well last night?

10:00.130 --> 10:01.810
I guess so.

10:01.810 --> 10:04.330
You haven't gotten sick?

10:04.330 --> 10:07.580
You're still holding last year against me?

10:07.580 --> 10:10.210
No, just messing with you.

10:10.620 --> 10:14.900
The test has already started, 
but you don't seem to be in a hurry.

10:15.210 --> 10:17.850
It's not like running around 
recklessly will do me any good.

10:20.990 --> 10:22.510
I have F9.

10:23.130 --> 10:25.130
We must be on different tables, then.

10:25.860 --> 10:28.510
Not that I'm worried about you.

10:28.970 --> 10:31.270
Try to finish the test with 
as high a rank as you can.

10:31.590 --> 10:36.160
I'd like to, but we could end 
up with the absurd result

10:36.160 --> 10:37.900
where I'm the only one expelled.

10:38.200 --> 10:40.360
I would certainly prefer to avoid that.

10:41.070 --> 10:44.160
I lent you quite a few 
points recently, after all.

10:44.160 --> 10:45.870
That's your objection?

10:46.220 --> 10:50.940
I know you're hurting for money due 
to your contract with Kushida-san,

10:50.940 --> 10:54.390
but giving her half your points 
every month was too far.

10:54.750 --> 10:56.850
I really do hate thinking about it.

10:57.180 --> 10:58.850
Just don't push yourself too hard.

10:59.190 --> 11:02.420
You have a hard fight 
ahead, as a lone woman.

11:02.420 --> 11:05.390
I choose to appreciate the warning.

11:06.170 --> 11:08.770
None of the second-year groups 
seem to be panicking.

11:09.160 --> 11:12.670
The first-years got to leave first, 
and we're over ten minutes behind.

11:13.070 --> 11:18.010
There's no point in burning stamina 
racing to the first designated area.

11:20.750 --> 11:24.780
Does Koenji really intend to take first?

11:24.780 --> 11:25.890
I don't know.

11:26.270 --> 11:31.920
I did make that bet with him, but I 
never know what he'll end up doing.

11:32.570 --> 11:35.390
There's no way to enforce a promise, yeah.

11:35.390 --> 11:39.550
All right! We can still take first place!

11:39.860 --> 11:42.940
Hurry it up, Nishino! Tsube, you too!

11:42.940 --> 11:46.140
Quit pushing me! It's too damn hot!

11:46.470 --> 11:49.810
It's not like we can catch 
up to the first-years now.

11:50.040 --> 11:52.520
Well, not with that attitude, we won't!

11:52.810 --> 11:56.110
They might let their guard down, too!

11:56.110 --> 11:59.620
Knock it off. It's a 
huge waste of stamina.

11:59.620 --> 12:01.520
Why not go without us?

12:01.520 --> 12:05.030
But then we won't get the 
arrival order reward!

12:05.030 --> 12:07.010
And it'd take forever to 
find each other after!

12:07.830 --> 12:08.540
There you are!

12:12.060 --> 12:13.230
Can I help you?

12:13.230 --> 12:15.040
Certainly not.

12:15.300 --> 12:16.670
I just want you to know...

12:16.980 --> 12:18.740
I won't let you beat me.

12:21.570 --> 12:24.940
Does she even realize how 
difficult this test is?

12:24.940 --> 12:27.800
She does seem quite motivated, at least.

12:28.250 --> 12:30.350
It's good to have a rival.

12:30.660 --> 12:33.190
Even if I don't see her that way at all.

12:33.630 --> 12:36.950
I'm relieved that she and I seem 
to have different tables, at least.

12:37.880 --> 12:38.930
Now, then.

12:39.660 --> 12:41.340
I'll be on my way.

12:54.140 --> 12:56.910
<i>One of the keys to this test</i>

12:56.910 --> 13:00.520
<i>is not to lose out on 
designated area game points.</i>

13:01.450 --> 13:04.130
<i>Placing highly in arrival 
rewards and challenges</i>

13:04.450 --> 13:07.760
<i>can get you five or ten 
points all at once,</i>

13:07.760 --> 13:11.720
<i>but that requires significant 
stamina, brains, and luck.</i>

13:12.410 --> 13:16.850
<i>That's why it's important to steadily 
rack up those basic arrival game points.</i>

13:18.250 --> 13:20.670
Are you talking about your next area?

13:21.240 --> 13:22.700
Hey, Kiyo-pon.

13:23.060 --> 13:26.580
Our first area is D8 here.

13:26.580 --> 13:28.350
So we're already done.

13:28.700 --> 13:30.530
What's your area, Kiyotaka?

13:30.530 --> 13:32.580
D7, one space north.

13:32.580 --> 13:34.480
Too bad we're not on the same table.

13:34.480 --> 13:36.880
We could've gone together.

13:36.880 --> 13:38.740
There are twelve of them, after all.

13:38.740 --> 13:42.130
I think I'll go clear my 
area as quickly as I can.

13:42.130 --> 13:43.770
We'll miss you.

13:43.770 --> 13:46.860
I hope we can meet up and spend 
more time chatting sometime!

13:47.830 --> 13:51.320
<i>There are many ways to cooperate 
without being in the same group,</i>

13:52.100 --> 13:53.180
Take care!

13:52.420 --> 13:58.520
<i>but you have to avoid working with 
people who might slow you down.</i>

13:59.250 --> 14:02.670
<i>This is one time I'm glad to be 
on a different table from them.</i>

14:09.420 --> 14:11.840
<i>Maybe I should move closer to the center</i>

14:11.840 --> 14:14.140
<i>in anticipation of the 
next designated area.</i>

14:15.940 --> 14:21.450
<i>To identify my rivals on the same table, 
I'll just have to go there and see.</i>

14:21.450 --> 14:22.840
Good morning.

14:23.380 --> 14:26.820
Nanase. Where are Hosen and Amasawa?

14:26.820 --> 14:29.090
They're investigating the area.

14:29.450 --> 14:34.350
I decided to see how many 
other groups were here.

14:34.580 --> 14:36.490
<i>That's the same thing I'm doing.</i>

14:37.140 --> 14:41.370
I'm sure it won't be easy by 
yourself. Please, take care.

14:41.870 --> 14:43.350
Excuse me.

14:46.330 --> 14:49.470
<i>I have three hours until the next 
designated area is announced.</i>

14:50.610 --> 14:54.740
<i>I can either wait here 
or head for a challenge.</i>

14:59.510 --> 15:02.130
Hey there, Ayanokoji-kun!

15:02.130 --> 15:04.100
Fancy seeing you here.

15:04.100 --> 15:05.630
But too bad...

15:05.630 --> 15:08.970
Registration closed five minutes ago.

15:08.970 --> 15:11.000
I see that.

15:11.000 --> 15:13.470
Don't be so quick to leave.

15:13.700 --> 15:15.720
You're free to watch if you'd like.

15:15.720 --> 15:21.480
I'm not sure teachers are supposed to 
be forcibly taking up students' time.

15:21.480 --> 15:24.530
Hey, that's not nice.

15:24.530 --> 15:28.490
I just wanted to talk a bit.

15:29.500 --> 15:33.740
We haven't talked like this 
since last year's final exam.

15:33.740 --> 15:34.990
True.

15:34.990 --> 15:38.710
You sure have been getting 
a lot of attention lately.

15:38.710 --> 15:41.760
I always thought you 
didn't like to stand out.

15:41.760 --> 15:43.500
I don't.

15:43.500 --> 15:47.960
Then why get that perfect score in math?

15:47.960 --> 15:50.510
It was quite remarkable.

15:50.510 --> 15:54.270
I think there are any number 
of students at the school who

15:54.270 --> 15:56.370
could solve problems like those.

15:56.370 --> 15:59.270
You think so? I wonder...

15:59.270 --> 16:03.270
Even if there were, you're in Class D.

16:03.270 --> 16:09.530
Should someone as talented 
as you be stuck down there?

16:09.530 --> 16:14.450
I think there are many talented 
students in Class 2-D.

16:14.450 --> 16:16.610
In Class 1-D, too.

16:17.080 --> 16:19.650
True, but still...

16:20.230 --> 16:24.670
I feel like the school's changed 
a lot since last year, huh?

16:26.170 --> 16:29.220
There are definitely 
excellent students there.

16:29.220 --> 16:32.920
But not at the level to move 
the needle on their classes...

16:32.920 --> 16:37.430
or change the environment around 
them, like you seem to be doing.

16:37.830 --> 16:42.820
<i>It sounds like she's been gathering 
a lot of information behind my back.</i>

16:43.180 --> 16:46.830
I'm really feeling desperate these days.

16:46.830 --> 16:49.960
I've never been dropped to Class C before.

16:49.960 --> 16:54.110
I really thought these kids 
could make it to Class A, too.

16:54.110 --> 16:57.700
Isn't dealing with that 
your job as a teacher?

16:58.190 --> 17:00.200
That hurts to hear.

17:00.690 --> 17:03.960
Hey, here's an out-of-the-box idea...

17:03.960 --> 17:09.590
Just like Katsuragi-kun joined Class B, 
would you like to join our class?

17:09.590 --> 17:12.360
That's an outrageous proposal.

17:12.360 --> 17:15.590
Let's aim for Class A together! Okay?

17:15.590 --> 17:20.670
I'll never get 20 million 
points before graduation.

17:21.090 --> 17:26.230
And at the moment, there's no telling 
which class will end up as Class A.

17:26.230 --> 17:29.900
Y-You don't have to spell 
it all out that coldly.

17:32.570 --> 17:35.530
Sudo-kun's changed a lot, hasn't he?

17:35.990 --> 17:37.950
I wonder who's behind that.

17:38.730 --> 17:41.460
Just so you know, it wasn't me.

17:41.780 --> 17:44.180
Now, I should be getting back.

17:45.240 --> 17:49.380
I'll be all over the 
place during the test,

17:49.660 --> 17:51.460
so we might see each other again!

17:57.130 --> 17:58.230
Senpai...

17:58.980 --> 18:00.270
We meet again.

18:00.660 --> 18:02.700
Yes. Quite a coincidence.

18:03.090 --> 18:04.890
How did you do today?

18:04.890 --> 18:08.600
Just getting three game points through 
arrival bonuses took everything I had.

18:08.930 --> 18:09.900
How about you?

18:10.290 --> 18:12.730
The three of us got eight game 
points from designated areas.

18:12.730 --> 18:16.270
And we took first in a challenge, 
for a total of 13.

18:16.760 --> 18:18.890
Sounds like a strong start.

18:18.890 --> 18:19.940
Yes.

18:20.330 --> 18:21.180
Um...

18:22.120 --> 18:23.800
No, I should be going.

18:29.740 --> 18:33.050
<i>Even if Tsukishiro wants to expel me</i>

18:33.050 --> 18:36.670
<i>through orthodox means by forcing 
me into the bottom five,</i>

18:37.110 --> 18:39.610
<i>I have control over how 
many game points I get.</i>

18:40.150 --> 18:43.430
<i>Instead, he may tamper 
with my watch or tablet</i>

18:43.670 --> 18:47.430
<i>to display false game point totals...</i>

18:48.350 --> 18:53.270
<i>But that plan will fall apart 
if I complain to the school.</i>

18:55.700 --> 18:58.340
<i>If he's using the White Room student,</i>

18:58.340 --> 19:01.870
<i>he may aim to disqualify me 
through injury or sickness.</i>

19:02.500 --> 19:07.510
<i>In other words, I'll be attacked in 
an area that isn't strictly monitored.</i>

19:08.730 --> 19:11.580
<i>That's a more realistic 
way to have me expelled.</i>

19:22.290 --> 19:24.360
E8, huh?

19:34.570 --> 19:38.180
<i>Given the time to make the trip, 
it might be best to let that one go.</i>

19:44.430 --> 19:45.980
<i>Second place twice in a row...</i>

19:46.820 --> 19:49.970
<i>I may have a powerful rival on my table.</i>

19:50.930 --> 19:53.310
<i>I guess I'll go back to E6 
and wait for a challenge.</i>

19:58.340 --> 19:59.890
Ayanokoji-senpai.

20:00.910 --> 20:02.630
We meet again.

20:02.980 --> 20:06.600
I wonder if we're on the same table.

20:06.600 --> 20:08.100
It's possible.

20:08.920 --> 20:11.050
<i>Even if we're heading to the same areas,</i>

20:11.410 --> 20:14.300
<i>the chance of running into 
each other so often seems low.</i>

20:14.820 --> 20:17.870
<i>It could be a series 
of coincidences, or...</i>

20:18.730 --> 20:21.940
Excuse me, Senpai. 
I have a favor to ask you.

20:22.260 --> 20:23.490
A favor?

20:24.130 --> 20:28.540
If I wouldn't be in the way, 
could I travel with you for a while?

20:29.380 --> 20:32.040
Travel with you? What do you mean?

20:32.300 --> 20:36.190
Last night, Hosen-kun and 
Amasawa-san said they were

20:36.190 --> 20:38.390
going off on their own for a while,

20:38.390 --> 20:40.660
and we split up.

20:40.660 --> 20:43.550
That could be a legitimate 
strategy, I suppose.

20:44.030 --> 20:48.810
I don't think I'll be able to keep up 
with the designated areas by myself.

20:49.330 --> 20:54.040
I've run into you three 
times since yesterday,

20:54.040 --> 20:57.940
and except for the first time, 
you've always arrived before me.

20:58.420 --> 21:03.620
Working with a group from a different 
year doesn't seem like a smart strategy.

21:04.120 --> 21:07.570
If we reach a challenge where only 
one more group can participate,

21:07.570 --> 21:10.100
it's liable to lead to a fight.

21:10.620 --> 21:13.830
I'm happy to defer to you in those cases.

21:14.540 --> 21:17.820
You'll be giving up game points.

21:18.190 --> 21:21.090
This is my first island special test.

21:21.370 --> 21:24.010
It would be a big help for 
me if you would just guide me

21:24.010 --> 21:25.840
through the best routes.

21:26.280 --> 21:31.750
Even if I know the best routes, 
can you keep up with me?

21:32.650 --> 21:34.870
I do have stamina.

21:35.350 --> 21:39.020
This feels less about my capabilities 
and more about a lack of trust.

21:40.780 --> 21:42.050
Very well.

21:42.050 --> 21:45.270
If that's what you want, 
you can come along.

21:45.270 --> 21:46.820
Thank you very much.

21:47.470 --> 21:49.340
What should we do from here on?

21:49.340 --> 21:52.100
We have over an hour before 
the area designation.

21:52.500 --> 21:56.200
There's a quiz challenge 
to the southeast, in F8.

21:56.200 --> 21:57.230
I'm heading for that.

21:57.810 --> 22:00.350
Very well. I'll come with you.
